joining us now Senate Judiciary  Committee chairman Lindsey Graham first  of all your overall overall reaction  it's very hard I guess everything for  the next 237 days Lindsey is going to be  viewed through the prism of politics in  her presidential election that is the  nature of politics this should be  something that's not political but it  has been politicized let's be honest no  president ever acted faster president  was criticized for the travel ban  criticized for the quarantine criticized  no matter what he did on this particular  thing immediately gave us eight point  three billion dollars set up the task  force I gave a rundown timeline of all  things and he's still getting hit well  if you want to play the criticism game  almost every Democrat came out hard  against President Trump when he shut  down travel from China the probably  strongest decision he's made the most  important decision was to act early when  he saw what was happening in China but  the president said tonight this is about  us as a nation not me as a president not  my party it's about all of us so he gave  an economic vaccine if we will follow  his lead I'm not so sure about the  payroll tax yet but everything else he  said made sense to me to stabilize the  economy and prevent the spread of the  virus I think the president was  incredibly presidential tonight he was  reassuring he's doing everything he can  in my view to stop the spread of the  virus we're taking it serious but we're  not gonna go crazy all right let's go  through what the president's been saying  tonight he'll always put the well-being  in the American people first if we are  vigilant we will significantly impede  the transmission of the virus no nation  is better prepared than the US all we  are all in this together put politics  aside which would be good for once you  put the travel ban to Europe for 30 days  with the exception of the UK emergency  actions providing financial relief for  businesses directly impacted I guess the  the cruise industry the airline industry  and workers by the way hourly paid  workers so they won't lose their jobs  and they'll have some financial relief  if they have to stay out for caution  anything else he should be doing in your  view  I can't really think of anything I know  this if President Obama had given this  same speech they would be applauding all  over the country for decisive leadership  clear-eyed view of the problem taking  action preventive action trying to bring  about economic stability before it gets  worse  trying to prevent the spread of the  virus I hope that everybody listening  tonight saw a president who was in  command of the issue in charge ready to  do whatever's necessary to stabilize the  economy and protect the American people  and I would just say this of all the  economies in the world were the  strongest and of all the places in the  world to provide quality health care  America is the premiere spot on the  planet and we're going to stay that way  let's talk about a there is a need for  some perspective I've been trying to  give it for example in a year with  12,000 Americans with h1n1 this is  2009-10 this isn't about politics what  I'm saying here but 12,000 Americans  died 20,000 contracted the disease there  was never a travel ban there was never  any type of quarantine put in place  there was not this level of alarmism  even the markets didn't react this  particular way I've never seen a  president instinctively put a ban in  place take a lot of heat for it  why if the flu is my pure numbers much  more dangerous why do you think there's  this reaction that we see everywhere  which we should take it and we ought to  take everything seriously I want to cure  for cancer and heart disease for the flu  for a common cold and for a corona of  course we've got to be careful I think  the exotic nature of it it came out of  China it came from left field nobody  really understands exactly what it's all  about yet a coronavirus case is like an  airplane crash the flu is like a car  wreck we have a lot of car wrecks people  down car wrecks but it doesn't get much  coverage every time somebody gets  infected with a car on reverse it's like  an airplane crash and that's just the  way the media has treated this they  treat the coronavirus like a series of  airplane crashes and all I can say about  the president if you've got a better  idea come forward and what I hope he  will do is not sign off of some  democratic package coming out of the  house  else tomorrow that's not going to grow  the economy but will grow the size of  the government we don't need economic  stimulus for the federal government we  need economic stimulus for the federal  offer for the for the American people  and they're going to want to grow  government and what the president wants  to do is help the economy well and I  think this is an important thing now the  president's right I mean bringing all  these bankers and Wall Street guys in I  think is a private-sector repo they were  it listen we have had the greatest  economic growth we've had we see the  jittery markets reacting day by day to  what is going on here there's the added  factor of a oil battle if you will  between Russia and the Saudis and OPEC  that does not help things but at the end  of the day we've had an unprecedented  economic growth now the question is if  we can keep these numbers low local  cities local states municipalities doing  their things schools closing as they  deem necessary people take in the  precautions they can take at the end of  the day what we have is a virus that's  very scary like every other virus but it  is unlike h1n1 H that impacted younger  people this seems to really be impacting  or putting it real risk only the elderly  with underlying health issues and some  type of immune disorders how do you  interpret that data well what what I  understand is that this is targeted to  the people who suffer the most or older  people people pre-existing conditions so  I don't think we've had anybody in the  world die under 30 let's take it serious  but the president is meeting with the  private sector he's asking banks to be  involved he wants to increase the amount  of money the Small Business  Administration can loan to people to get  back on their feet look and see what  Democrats do tomorrow I think they're  going to grow government programs they  haven't talked to anybody in the private  sector about what we can do to stabilize  the economy their reaction unfortunately  is going to go going to be to grow the  government the president's action is try  to create a partnership between the  government in the private sector to  stabilize the economy and he realized  more than anybody any president in my  life  that the strength of the American  economy and American people is in the  private sector not our government  all right Senator Lindsey Graham thank  you tonight

